From ed1c4e7c9effa655a8b675f3374eec88beb17133 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: albanread <albanread@googlemail.com>
Date: Mon, 21 Sep 2026 16:03:01 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] Platinum: a window frame after Mac OS 8.5, and a theme with
 it

A new decorator. A bevelled grey frame inside a dark outline, the frame
standing proud of the content with an inner line round it; a title bar
grooved with fine lines from the close box to the zoom box, stopping
short of the centred title; a plain square close box at the left, zoom
and collapse boxes at the right, each sunk in a well (collapse
minimizes); a grow box with ridges in a document window's corner. A
window in the background goes flat and loses its grooves and boxes, as
it did there, and a click where a box was only brings the window
forward. Floating windows get a thinner frame and smaller boxes, modal
ones the frame with no bar.

It is drawn in whole units that grow with the system font (two pixels
on this machine's), so it stays pixel art on a dense screen, and its
greys are tints of the system's tab colour, so a theme can tint it. The
layout is ProseDecorator's, except that the top border is drawn as the
lower part of the title bar: every border stays as wide as BorderWidth()
says, which stack and tile and BWindow::DecoratorFrame() count on.

Platinum.theme puts it together with platinum grey panels and menus, a
lavender highlight and dark blue menu selections, on a plain periwinkle
desktop with no picture.

Verified in a guest with a test program opening one window of each
look: the active and inactive bars, the modal and floating frames and
the grow box drawn as intended; a click on a background window's close
box brought it forward and left it open, collapse minimized, zoom on a
background window only activated it and a second click zoomed it.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
